window.docContents[56].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Mm.Mprotect/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Mm___Mprotect":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Mm › Mprotect.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 57 of 85 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nLinux mprotect SyscallDefines SYS_MPROTECT (226) and execMprotect, modeling Linux 7.3 do_mprotect_pkey (mm/mprotect.c:892) for PROT_NONE and PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE on non-frozen mapped memory.\n\n\n\ndef SYS_MPROTECTL26–27 ↗#Linux AArch64 mprotect syscall number (__NR_mprotect = 226, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:616, mm/mprotect.c:892).\n\ndef execMprotectL29–86 ↗#Minimal mprotect(addr, len, prot) (__NR_mprotect = 226, mm/mprotect.c:892 do_mprotect_pkey) for PROT_NONE (0x0) and PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE (0x3) on non-frozen mapped memory. With size := pageAlignUp len:* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: if prot is neither MMAP_PROT_NONE (0) nor MMAP_PROT_RW (3), fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled mprotect (only PROT_NONE and PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE)\";* if addr is not page-aligned (addr.toNat % PAGE_SIZE != 0), returns -EINVAL;* if [addr, addr + size) exceeds the 48-bit user virtual address space (addr.toNat + size > 2 ^ 48), fails closed with .Exception \"mprotect range exceeds user VA space\";* if len == 0, returns 0 without modifying memory (mm/mprotect.c:821);* if [addr, addr + size) intersects any frozen byte, fails closed with .Exception \"mprotect on frozen memory\";* if [addr, addr + size) is completely unmapped (s.mem.canMap addr size), returns -ENOMEM without modifying memory (matching Linux mm/mprotect.c:854 when the first page has no VMA);* if [addr, addr + size) mixes mapped and unmapped bytes (!s.mem.allPerm (·.mapped) addr size and !s.mem.canMap addr size), fails closed with .Exception \"mprotect on partially mapped range\";* otherwise updates the permission of every byte in [addr, addr + size) to Perm.protNone (when prot == MMAP_PROT_NONE, with 0 refund to s.physMemAvail because setPermNonFrozen retains resident byte values and Linux mprotect_fixup in mm/mprotect.c:819-820 does not un-account resident anonymous pages on write-removal) or Perm.rw (when prot == MMAP_PROT_RW, charging needed := size - s.mem.countRw addr size against s.physMemAvail and transitioning to ExecStatus.OutOfMemory if s.physMemAvail < needed), preserving byte values, and returns 0.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Mm/Mprotect.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Mm.Mprotect/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Mm___Mprotect"}});